# Waitlist — src/components/WaitlistCta.tsx
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED. The live Google Form URL is committed in the
# component, so the site deploys and the waitlist works with no configuration.
# That is deliberate: the URL is a link visitors click, there is nothing to keep
# secret, and a required variable would let the site ship in a state where the
# one action on the page goes nowhere.
#
# Set this only to point a deployment at a DIFFERENT form — a preview
# environment you do not want mixed into the real responses, or a separate
# Korean-language form later.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ because it is read at render time and inlined into the page, so
# changing it needs a redeploy. Never put anything secret behind that prefix.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WAITLIST_FORM_URL=https://forms.gle/xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# ── Where the responses go ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The form's Responses tab should be linked to a Sheet, which is the review
# queue for picking the ~10 beta channels. That Sheet holds personal data:
# email addresses and channel links given for one purpose. Keep it inside the
# sudo-cut.com Workspace, share it per-person rather than by link, and delete
# rows on request.
